# The repo carries the game and its dev tools (tests in tools/, simbot.py, simlib.py, simreport.py and the check scripts),
# so a fresh clone can run the suite. What stays out: anything your play writes, anything a build or a tool regenerates,
# and local environments.

# --- What the game writes while you play: your campaigns and session logs (audit, turns, refusals, model calls) ---
saves/
logs/
recordings/
*.log

# --- (f522) The model server's builds, the model files and the game's run files: fetched or written, never kept ---
/runtime/
/models/
/run/

# --- Build output: build_exe.bat and build_installer.bat recreate these ---
build/
dist/
*.spec
installer/Output/
installer/models.iss   # (f531) written by build_installer.bat from data/runtime/server.yaml

# --- Local Python environments and caches (play.bat makes .venv on first run) ---
.venv/
.buildenv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- What the dev tools write: the tools themselves are tracked, their output is not ---
/sim_out*/
/lora/
/sim_report*
/sim_*.txt
/boss_transcript.md

# --- Sandbox scratch: run scripts with a hard-coded Linux path, no use on another machine ---
/runbal.sh
/runfull*.sh

# --- OS and editor clutter ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Claude Code: the full-suite pass marker for this machine (.claude/hooks/known.py --mark), and each person's own settings ---
/.claude/.suite_passed
/.claude/settings.local.json
